The permit requirements of this article shall not apply to:
(1) Funeral processions formed and conducted in accordance with O.C.G.A. § 40-6-76(a);
(2) A government entity or agency acting within the scope of its legal authority, duties and functions;
(3) On not less than 24 hours' notice from the event organizer, the city manager shall have the discretion to waive the requirement for a permit for a spontaneous exercise of First Amendment rights, provided such exercise is wholly located on city controlled property located at 600 Lee Avenue, being a tract of approximately 11.8 acres. This exception is provided to afford an alternative adequate avenue for communications protected by the First Amendment. In order to exercise the discretion afforded by this section, the city manager, or his designee, shall meet, in person, in advance, with the event organizer in order to determine the level of security required for citizens and property during the event.
(Ord. No. 2020-395, § 3, 6-18-2020)

