(a) In order to ensure the safety of those traveling through the city on its rights-of-way, all impeding of the flow of traffic and all parking in unmarked parking spaces is prohibited.
(b) As to certain portions of specific rights-of-way, petitions may be made in advance to the city council for a permit to impede traffic and park outside designated parking spaces, for either a fundraiser or another special event of some kind (including, but not limited to, such events as parades, bike races, Christmas in the Street, antique car shows, and motorcycle club gatherings). They are as follows:
(1) State Route 341: from the intersection of Euclid Avenue north to the intersection of West Ninth Street;
(2) Gordon Street: from the intersection of Wilder Avenue east to West Tenth Street;
(3) West Tenth Street to Crittenden Avenue;
(4) Thomas Avenue: from the intersection of Gordon Street north to the intersection of West Seventh Street;
(5) West Ninth Street: from the intersection of Thomas Avenue to the intersection of State Route 341.
(c) As to any rights-of-way which are physically outside of the designated areas set forth in subsection (b) of this section, anyone wanting to either impede the flow of traffic or to park somewhere within the right-of-way where there is not a designated parking place for the purpose of some type of special event, must obtain permission from the chief of police in order to do so.
(Ord. No. 2008-269, art. I, § 1, 7-7-2008)
